  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "1 · Parse (tree-sitter)",
      "items": [
        "`def pay(...)` is a function_definition node; its decorator @router.post(...) sits on the parent decorated_definition",
        "Every `call` node gives Call {name, line}; `raise_statement` gives Raise; each `except_clause` gives Handler {types, try range, action}",
        "The extractor walks the tree once and returns FileFacts: imports, Symbols, env reads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "2 · Build (pure, no database)",
      "items": [
        "file_graph turns one file's Symbols into File / Function / Class / Route / LogStatement / Chunk nodes",
        "Ids carry no line numbers, e.g. sym:orders:app/main.py:pay, so an edit keeps the same node",
        "Facts that need other files (calls, HTTP calls, imports, queue and SQL ops) are stored on the node as properties"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "3 · Store (incremental)",
      "items": [
        "Only added or changed files are parsed; nodes are upserted, never deleted and recreated",
        "Then every link edge is recomputed from node properties by graph::link",
        "Steps run in one transaction; then reconcile marks Knowledge stale or orphaned"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
